# UI

Emulocke visual direction is **graphite clamshell**: matte graphite chassis, inset screen wells, parchment-metal hairlines (`#D7CDBD`), metal text on dark, scarce crimson for pause only. Type is M PLUS Rounded 1c for display and Fira Sans for body. Blocky DS geometry. Not cream command boxes. Not stock ImGui gray. Not purple gradients. Not Inter/Roboto/Arial/system UI fonts.

Screens sit in bezels. The left column stays the home pane size; screens integer-scale inside it. 5px DS hinge when the pane allows. 21px graphite around the column. Suite is a tab bar on a recessed rail; the selected tab is a raised plate, not the same fill as the pane. Tracker is first, Pokémon second, Calculator third, Cheats fourth, Logs fifth. With no run seated, only Logs is shown. Cart status stays in Logs, never above START RUN or in New Run. Integer-scale nearest-neighbor for emulator pixels. No scanlines. Tracker rows are graphite inset plates with box sprites, not nuzlocke.app purple. Red is pause and destructive, not hover.

Compact chrome: primary click targets stay named. Secondary actions in dense chrome are icons; the full name lives on hover. Do not spend a label column on an action that is not the primary hit. Menus stay labeled text.
